00:04:45,714 --> 00:04:51,714
No booze. No sex. No drugs. No way.

2
00:09:31,428 --> 00:09:37,428
Sister Act is a music, comedy film directed by Emile Ardolino.

3
00:14:17,142 --> 00:14:23,142
A Reno singer witnesses a mob murder and the cops stash her in a
nunnery to protect her from the mob's hitmen.

4
00:19:02,857 --> 00:19:08,857
The mother superior does not trust her, and takes steps
to limit her influence on the other nuns.

5
00:23:48,571 --> 00:23:54,571
Eventually the singer rescues the failing choir and begins helping with community
projects, which gets her an interview on TV—and identification by the mob.

6
00:28:34,285 --> 00:28:40,285
Deloris Van Cartier / Sister Mary Clarence, played by Whoopi Goldberg.

7
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Mother Superior, played by Maggie Smith.

8
00:38:05,714 --> 00:38:11,714
Sister Mary Patrick, played by Kathy Najimy.

9
00:42:51,428 --> 00:42:57,428
Sister Mary Robert, played by Wendy Makkena.

10
00:47:37,142 --> 00:47:43,142
Sister Mary Lazarus, played by Mary Wickes.

11
00:52:22,857 --> 00:52:28,857
Vince LaRocca, played by Harvey Keitel.

12
00:57:08,571 --> 00:57:14,571
Sister Act is a 1992 American musical crime comedy film directed by Emile
Ardolino and written by Paul Rudnick (billed as Joseph Howard).

13
01:01:54,285 --> 01:02:00,285
It stars Whoopi Goldberg as a lounge singer forced to hide in a
convent after being placed in a witness protection program.

14
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
It also features Maggie Smith, Kathy Najimy, Wendy
Makkena, Mary Wickes, and Harvey Keitel.

15
01:11:25,714 --> 01:11:31,714
Receiving mixed to favorable reviews, Sister Act was one of the most financially successful comedies
of the early 1990s, grossing $231.6 million worldwide against a $31 million budget.

16
01:16:11,428 --> 01:16:17,428
Its success extended to the home video market, and it was the
most rented film of 1993 in the United States.

17
01:20:57,142 --> 01:21:03,142
The film spawned a franchise, which consists of the critically panned 1993 sequel Sister
Act 2: Back in the Habit and a musical adaptation, which premiered in 2006.

18
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
A third film is in development for Disney+.

19
01:30:28,571 --> 01:30:34,571
The film explores themes of concert, nun, church
choir, witness protection, gospel.

20
01:35:14,285 --> 01:35:20,285
The tone is lighthearted.
